      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Nazanin,\n\nThanks for your patient and quick explanation.\nI appreciate that very much.\n\nDo you mean that at line#170, numOfSims is saved as argument arg1 in message?\nIf we look at the Message.obtain function, there is no below function:\npublic static Message obtain(Handler h, int what, int arg1)\n\nBut there is only below function instead:\npublic static Message obtain(Handler h, int what, Object obj)\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/Message.java#213\n\nSo as my understanding, numOfSims is passed as msg.obj instead of msg.arg1.\n\nAnd for your comment: \"msg.obj contains the return value\", I missed this point.\nAt this place, msg.obj should be AsyncResult instead of numOfLiveModems.\n\nSo I think here to handle EVENT_SWITCH_DSDS_CONFIG_DONE, we should use below code logic:\n\n@Override\npublic void handleMessage(Message msg) {\n    AsyncResult ar;\n    switch (msg.what) {\n        case EVENT_SWITCH_DSDS_CONFIG_DONE: {\n            ar \u003d (AsyncResult)msg.obj;\n            Integer numOfLiveModems \u003d (Integer)ar.userObj;\n            // Only when exception is null and result is presented,\n            // we can update the multi sim properties.\n            if (ar.exception \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 ar.result !\u003d null) {\n                setMultiSimProperties(numOfLiveModems);\n            } else {\n                log(msg.what + \" failure. Not switching multi-sim config.\");\n            }\n            break;\n        }\n        default:\n            break;\n    }\n}\n\nRefer below:\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/AdnRecordLoader.java#handleMessage\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/SubscriptionInfoUpdater.java#213\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java#3076\n\nNote that for normal switchMultiSimConfig case, ar.result is non-null, and should be RIL_REQUEST_SWITCH_DUAL_SIM_CONFIG.\nAs we pass RILRequest#request as result here:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfigResponse.java#191\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioResponse.java#sendMessageResponse\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/AsyncResult.java#36\n\nBelow is my understanding about detail sequence of switchMultiSimConfig.\nAnd as we can see AsyncResult(with numOfLiveModems as userObj) should always be returned here.\n1. Exception case\nFor exception case, it should be AsyncResult with userObj(numOfLiveModems) and Throwable:\nCase 1: Moible network is not supported, or IRadioConfig is unavailable\na) RadioConfig#setModemsConfig triggers RadioConfig#getRadioConfigProxy\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfig.java#412\nb) In RadioConfig#getRadioConfigProxy it returns AsyncResult with userObj(numOfLiveModems) and Throwable\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfig.java#167\nMoible network is not supported\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfig.java#171\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/AsyncResult.java#36\nor IRadioConfig is unavailable\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfig.java#186\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/AsyncResult.java#36\n\nCase 2: IRadioConfig available, but modem returns exception:\na) Receive modem response:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfigResponse.java#186\n\nb) Then trigger RILRequest#onError to send AsyncResult with userObj(numOfLiveModems), response(should be null) and Throwable:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfigResponse.java#195\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RILRequest.java#onError\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/AsyncResult.java#36\n\n2. Normal set modem config case:\na) Receive modem response:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfigResponse.java#186\n\nb) Then trigger RadioResponse#sendMessageResponse to send AsyncResult userObj(numOfLiveModems) and result(RIL_REQUEST_SWITCH_DUAL_SIM_CONFIG)\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/890295/4/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioConfigResponse.java#214\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioResponse.java#sendMessageResponse\nhttp://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/AsyncResult.java#36\n\nPlease correct me if I missed any point.\n\nThanks",
